---
title: Sesame & spring onion stir-fried udon with crispy tofu
servings: 4
course: dinner
image: https://images.immediate.co.uk/production/volatile/sites/30/2020/10/Sesame-spring-onion-stir-fried-udon-with-crispy-tofu-2801160.jpg?resize=900,836
tags: quick, noodle, tofu, vegetarian
source: https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/sesame-spring-onion-stir-fried-udon-with-crispy-tofu
time: 20m
---

Drain and pat the @firm tofu{400%g} dry with kitchen paper. Cut into cubes, wrap in more kitchen paper, and place a heavy board over the top. Leave to drain for ~{15%minutes}.

Mix the @cornflour{1%tbsp}, @chilli flake{0.5-1%tsp} and @szechuan peppercorn{0.25-0.5%tsp} ground together in a #bowl{} with a pinch of salt, then add the drained @&firm tofu{}. Toss well to coat.

Heat half the @vegetable oil{0.5%tbsp} in a large #frying pan{} over a high heat, and fry the @&firm tofu{} pieces for ~{5-6%minutes} until golden all over. Scoop out of the #&frying pan{}, and leave to drain on kitchen paper.

Add the remaining @&vegetable oil{0.5%tbsp} to the #&frying pan{} and stir-fry the @spring onion{1%bunch} and @green bean{200%g} for ~{3-4%minutes} until tender and lightly golden. Pour a kettle of boiling water over the @udon noodle{400%g} in a #sieve{} to loosen. Drain well, then tip into the #&frying pan{}. Fry for a few minutes until piping hot. Add the @sesame oil{0.5%tbsp} and @sesame seed{2%tsp}, and sizzle for a few seconds. Splash in the @soy sauce{1%tbsp}, @rice vinegar{1%tbsp}, then add the @&firm tofu{}. Toss well, then serve in bowls with a pinch of @&sesame seed{} on top and more @&soy sauce{} on the side.
